# ALSA overrides for headless runs.
#
# Loaded via XDG_CONFIG_HOME: the hook at the top of
# /usr/share/alsa/alsa.conf loads, in order, /etc/alsa/conf.d,
# /etc/asound.conf, ~/.asoundrc and finally
# $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/alsa/asoundrc. Last one wins, which is why the
# overrides live here and not in a file named by ALSA_CONFIG_PATH:
# definitions in that file are loaded *before* the hook runs, so
# /etc/alsa/conf.d/99-pipewire-default.conf overrides them and the
# whole exercise does nothing. Measured with amixer, not assumed.
#
# Why any of this is needed: with the pipewire socket unreachable, the
# ALSA pipewire plugin's failure path calls pw_thread_loop_stop(),
# which joins a loop thread nothing wakes, and the process hangs inside
# pjsua_init before any Comlink code runs. dpkg-buildpackage runs the
# suite without the operator's session, so it hits exactly that
# condition. See docs/known-issues.md.
#
# There are TWO paths into that plugin, and overriding only the first
# left the suite hanging again a few hours later:
#
#   1. pjmedia's get_mixer_name() calls
#      snd_mixer_attach(handle, "default"), and ctl.default is the
#      pipewire plugin on a desktop Debian box.
#   2. device enumeration probes named PCMs, so it opens pcm.pipewire,
#      pcm.pulse and pcm.jack directly, whatever "default" points at.
#
# So every sound-server namespace is redirected, not just default.
# Hardware devices still enumerate normally, which is what keeps
# pjmedia's audio subsystem valid: with no devices at all it fails with
# PJMEDIA_EAUD_SYSERR and pjsua_init fails outright.
#
# A card that may not exist is fine: pjmedia gives up on the mixer
# label and carries on. A plugin that hangs is not.

ctl.!default   { type hw card 0 }
pcm.!default   { type null }

ctl.!pipewire  { type hw card 0 }
pcm.!pipewire  { type null }

ctl.!pulse     { type hw card 0 }
pcm.!pulse     { type null }

pcm.!jack      { type null }
